The GPL grant is for our original contributions, not a blanket relicensing of
this repository or its downloadable historical runtime. In particular:

* Original MUD source/data at the repository root, the preserved source/
  archive, historical text/code quotations and generated MUD derivatives retain
  their original notices and upstream not-for-profit terms. See
  licenses/MUD1-NOTICE.txt. No not-for-profit restriction is added to our GPL code.
* web/vendor/ retains its per-component terms; see THIRD_PARTY.md.
* TOPS-10, DEC utilities, the Essex BCPL toolchain and native libraries retain
  their own terms. Permissions for our historical runtime redistribution remain
  unverified. Licensing our diagnostic source does not clear its linked binary
  or grant rights to the libraries it uses.
* SIMH and downloaded Python/system dependencies retain their own licences.
* Licence texts, quoted notices, provenance documents and third-party documents
  are not relicensed by this grant. Project-authored explanatory documentation
  may be redistributed with the restoration under GPL-3.0-only; incorporated
  third-party material remains under its own terms.

